## African drumming incursions FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question
   title="What ages are your African drumming incursions suitable for?" %}
Our African drumming incursions suit kindergartens, early learning centres, primary schools, high schools and vacation care programs. In addition, we adapt every session to the age and abilities of the group.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do we need to supply drums?" %}
No. Every student has a West African drum at no extra cost, because we bring all the instruments.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Which areas do you travel to?" %}
We visit schools across Australia, including the Sunshine Coast, Brisbane, Sydney, Melbourne, Perth and Adelaide. What's more, there are no travel fees.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How does the incursion link to the curriculum?" %}
It complements The Arts (Music and Dance) in the Australian Curriculum, as well as the General Capabilities and all five EYLF learning outcomes.
{% /question %}

{% question
   title="How long is a session and how many students can take part?" %}
Sessions run from 30 minutes to 1.5 hours, depending on group size, ages and activity. For example, we can run several back-to-back sessions with around 30 students in each. Otherwise, we can run one large session with all students together.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}

